@page "/"
@using BookHeaven.Web.Components
<PageTitle>Home | BookHeaven</PageTitle>

<CenteredPage>
	<section class="mb-10 md:mb-20 mx-auto max-w-[700px] text-center">
		<p class="mb-10 text-4xl font-bold text-white md:text-6xl">
			Take <span class="text-(--color-primary)">control</span><br/>of your digital library
		</p>
		<p class="mb-10 text-lg text-white md:text-2xl text-balance break-keep">
			BookHeaven is a tiny <span class="text-(--color-primary)">self-hosted</span> ecosystem that helps you manage and read your e-books in a very <span class="text-(--color-primary)">convenient</span> way.
		</p>
		<p class="mb-10 text-white md:mb-20 text-balance italic">Check out what each part of the ecosystem can do for you down below,<br class="sm:inline hidden"/> and press this button to make your life easier.</p>
		<a
			class="rounded-lg px-5 py-2 text-2xl font-bold text-white mx-auto bg-(--color-secondary) !no-underline transition-colors hover:bg-(--color-secondary)/70"
			href="/getting-started">
			Get Started
		</a>
	</section>
	<hr class="my-10 text-neutral-700 md:my-20"/>
	<section class="flex flex-col">
		<div class="gap-5 flex items-center justify-between">
			<h1 class="text-2xl font-bold md:text-4xl leading-none text-nowrap">BookHeaven <span class="text-(--color-primary)">Server</span></h1>
			<GithubButtonLink Url="https://github.com/BookHeaven/BookHeaven.Server" />
		</div>
		
		<div class="mt-3 gap-2 flex items-center">
			<Pill Text="web"/>
			<Pill Text="docker"/>
			<Pill Text="e-reader"/>
			<Pill Text="opds"/>
			<Pill Text="koreader sync"/>
		</div>
		<p class="my-5 ms-2 text-slate-300">
			Upload your e-books and organize them to your liking into authors, series, tags and collections. You can also upload fonts so your devices can download and use them.<br/>
			It's really easy to set up and use, and you can run it on any device that supports Docker.<br/>
		</p>
		<div class="mx-2 mt-5 md:mx-5 md:mt-10 relative">
			<img src="img/server-shelf.png" class="glow rounded-lg md:rounded-2xl border-2 border-(--color-primary)" alt=""/>
			<div class="-right-2 -bottom-2 rounded-xl bg-black p-1 outline-slate-700 md:-right-5 md:-bottom-5 md:w-2/12 md:p-2 absolute w-3/12 overflow-hidden outline">
				<img src="img/server-shelf-mobile.png" alt="" class="rounded-lg" />
			</div>
			
		</div>
		
	</section>
	<hr class="my-10 text-neutral-700 md:my-20"/>
	<section class="flex flex-col">
		<div class="gap-5 flex items-center justify-between">
			<h1 class="text-2xl font-bold md:text-4xl leading-none text-nowrap">BookHeaven <span class="text-(--color-primary)">Reader</span></h1>
			<GithubButtonLink Url="https://github.com/BookHeaven/BookHeaven.Reader" />
		</div>
		<div class="mt-3 gap-2 flex items-center">
			<Pill Text="android"/>
			<Pill Text="e-reader"/>
			<Pill Text="e-ink"/>
			<Pill Text="launcher"/>
		</div>
		<p class="my-5 ms-2 text-slate-300">
			If you have an android e-reader, you are in luck. With this app you'll be able to connect to your server and easily download and read all of your books.<br/>
			But not only that, it will also track your progress and reading time for each book, which you can manually sync to your server at any time.<br/>
			No connection required at all for regular use, so you can save your precious battery life.
		</p>
		<div class="glow mx-2 mt-5 gap-1 rounded-lg bg-black px-2 py-2 md:mx-5 md:mt-10 md:rounded-2xl md:px-5 md:py-5 grid grid-cols-3 overflow-hidden border-2 border-(--color-primary)">
			<img src="img/reader-books-home.png" class="grayscale" alt=""/>
			<img src="img/reader-books-shelf.png" class="grayscale" alt=""/>
			<img src="img/reader-book.png" class="grayscale" alt=""/>
			<img src="img/reader-highlights.png" class="grayscale" alt=""/>
			<img src="img/reader-highlights-list.png" class="grayscale" alt=""/>
			<img src="img/reader-temperature-settings.png" alt=""/>
			<img src="img/reader-index.png" class="grayscale" alt=""/>
			<img src="img/reader-text-settings.png" class="grayscale" alt=""/>
			<img src="img/reader-page-settings.png" class="grayscale" alt=""/>
		</div>
	</section>
</CenteredPage>